From be5d2ffcec46bb68ecb2e8f6e0d3b2c7c1082cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:32:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(xtask): end a silent gate step by itself and name it
 (STALL row)

The gate watches each step. A step whose process tree writes no output
for 15 minutes (60 for --release and --ignored steps;
CAMCRAFT_GATE_STALL_MIN overrides) is killed as a tree. The gate prints
STALL <m>min <step> with the last lines and the live processes, records
a STALL row, goes on, and exits 3 when only STALL rows are red.

post-merge.yml: the batch step has timeout-minutes 45 (the job cap of
90 stays), and the summary step marks a timeout. The report script
treats a STALL row or a timeout with no FAIL row as a runner stall: one
warning, no "main is red" issue. AGENTS.md gets the rule "Runner stops";
the gate and runners skills name the variable and the row.

Fixes #3303

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
